{"id": "EUVD-2026-91138", "enisaUuid": "46b97fe7-e752-3b13-b263-3722a53fc661", "description": "ClipBucket v5 through 5.5.3-#197 contains an sql injection vulnerability that allows authenticated users with ad_manager_access permission to inject SQL via the delete parameter in admin_area/ads_manager.php. Attackers can supply time-based blind payloads concatenated into AdsManager::DeleteAd queries to extract user credentials and emails or modify and delete arbitrary records.", "datePublished": "2026-10-01T23:20:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-06T13:36:59", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@leediay/sqli-via-delete-ads-clipbucketv5", "https://github.com/MacWarrior/clipbucket-v5/pull/925", "https://github.com/MacWarrior/clipbucket-v5/blob/f15cef1a2431786c31ffd79e81f55d6eeca4ebc0/upload/includes/classes/ads.class.php#L102-L110", "https://github.com/MacWarrior/clipbucket-v5", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/clipbucket-v5-through-5.5.3-197-sql-injection-via-ads-manager-php-delete-parameter"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-103766", "GHSA-29w7-pp39-xf4w"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "be7ecb73-9ac8-3132-a9f8-3de66785e297", "product": {"name": "clipbucket-v5", "vendor": {"name": "MacWarrior"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22645.5.3-#197"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8c6e1410-086f-3555-a17e-5620e0ae1668", "vendor": {"name": "MacWarrior"}}], "isExploited": false}